1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. b4 Bg7 4. Bb2 O-O 5. g3 d6 (5... a5 6. b5 c6 (6... b6 7. Bg2 Bb7 8. O-O d6 9. d3 Nbd7 10. Nd4 { Common idea with the outpost on c6 - get rid of their bishop controlling that square. } 10... Bxg2 11. Kxg2 e5 12. Nc6 Qe8 13. Nc3 Nb8 14. Nxb8 Rxb8 15. e4 Qd7 16. Qe2 { Todo: look into future plans }) (6... d5 7. cxd5 Qxd5 (7... Nxd5 8. Bxg7 Kxg7 9. Bg2 c6 10. Qb3 a4 11. Qb2+ Kg8 12. O-O cxb5 13. Qxb5 Nc6 14. Qb2) 8. a4 c6 9. Bg2 cxb5 10. Nc3 Qh5 11. Nxb5 Nc6 12. h3 Rd8 13. d4 { We can't castle yet due to the double attack on h3 }) 7. a4 d5 (7... cxb5 8. cxb5 b6 9. Bg2 Bb7 10. O-O d6 11. Na3 Nbd7 12. Nd4 { We go for the outpost on c6! 
And also get rid of the bishop that defends that square. } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gd4c6] } 12... Bxg2 13. Kxg2 Nc5 14. Nc6 Qd7 15. Nc4 Qb7 16. d4 Ne6 17. d5 { [%cal Gd5c6] }) 8. Bg2 dxc4 9. O-O cxb5 10. axb5 Nbd7 11. Na3 Nb6 12. Ne5 Qc7 13. Rc1 Be6 14. d3 Rfd8 15. Nexc4 { Black can't contiue the full sequence: (15... Nxc4 16. Nxc4 Bxc4 17. Rxc4 }) (5... d5 6. cxd5 Nxd5 (6... Qxd5 7. Bg2 Nc6 8. a3 Bf5 9. d3 a5 10. Nc3) 7. Bxg7 Kxg7 8. Qc1 { Protecting the pawn with Qb2+ fork } { [%cal Rd5b4,Rc1b2] } 8... Kg8 9. Bg2 Nxb4 10. O-O N8c6 11. Qb2 Bg4 12. Nc3 Rb8 13. Rfd1 Nd5 14. d4 { Todo: what is the actual compensation for the pawn }) (5... c6 6. Bg2 d5 7. cxd5 cxd5 8. O-O Nc6 (8... a6 9. a4 Nc6 10. b5 axb5 11. axb5 Rxa1 12. Bxa1 Na5 13. d3 b6 14. Qa4 Bb7 15. Rc1) 9. b5 Na5 10. d3 b6 11. Nbd2 Bb7 12. Nb3 Nxb3 13. Qxb3 Rc8 14. Rac1) (5... b6 6. Bg2 Bb7 7. Qb3 { Stopping c5 at least temporarily } 7... d5 8. O-O Nbd7 9. cxd5 Bxd5 10. Qc2 c5 11. bxc5 Nxc5 12. Nc3) (5... c5 6. bxc5 Qa5 { The most common move, but we respond the same in other variations - by leaving the pawn hanging.

For example: (6... Na6 7. Bg2 Nxc5 8. O-O d6 9. d3)

Even if black plays b6: (6... b6 7. Bg2 bxc5 8. Ne5 Nc6 9. Nxc6 dxc6 10. O-O no need to recapture the pawn yet) } { [%cal Bb8a6,Bb7b6,Bb8c6,Bf1g2] } 7. Bg2 Qxc5 8. Qb3 Nc6 9. O-O Na5 10. Qa3 Qxa3 11. Nxa3 { Candidates moves next are Bc3, Rab1, Nd5, d3 } { [%cal Bb2c3,Bd2d3,Ba1b1,Bf3d4] }) 6. Bg2 e5 (6... Nbd7 7. O-O c5 { [%cal Gd1b3] } 8. b5 a6 9. a4 axb5 10. cxb5 Nb6 11. d3 Bd7 12. Nfd2 { [%cal Gb1c3,Bd2c4,Ba4a5] }) 7. d3 Nc6 (7... c6 8. Nbd2 Nbd7 9. a3 Re8 10. O-O d5 11. cxd5 cxd5 12. e4 d4 (12... dxe4 13. dxe4 { If black allow us - we'll go for Nc4. } { [%csl Gc4][%cal Gd2c4] } 13... b6 (13... b5 { Stopping Nc4. } { [%cal Rd2c4] } 14. a4 { [%cal Gc8a6,Gd1e2,Bf1c1,Bf1d1] }) 14. Nc4 Ba6 15. Nd6 Bxf1 16. Bxf1 Rf8 17. Bc4 Qe7 18. Ng5 { [%csl Gf7][%cal Gg5f7] } 18... h6 19. Ngxf7 Kh7 20. Rc1) 13. Nc4 b5 14. Nd6 Re6 15. Nxf7 Kxf7 16. Ng5+ Ke7 17. Nxe6 Kxe6 18. f4) (7... a5 8. b5 Nbd7 9. O-O Nc5 10. Nc3 a4 11. Ba3 e4 12. Ne1 exd3 13. Nxd3 Nxd3 14. Qxd3 Re8 15. Rad1 Bf5 16. e4 Be6 17. f4) (7... Nbd7 8. O-O Re8 9. Nc3 e4 (9... c6 10. Nd2 Nf8 11. b5 Bd7 12. a4 Rc8 13. Ba3 Be6 14. Nde4 Nxe4 15. Nxe4) 10. Nxe4 Nxe4 11. Bxg7 Kxg7 { This is most common but black can also throw in a desperado:(11... Nxg3 12. hxg3 Kxg7 13. a4)(11... Nxf2 12. Rxf2 Kxg7 13. Qd2) } 12. dxe4 Rxe4 13. Nd4 Re8 14. e3) (7... Bg4 8. h3 Be6 { Also common to take the knight, but it looks like easy play for us: (9. Bxf3 c6 10. O-O Nbd7 11. Nc3) } 9. O-O Qd7 10. Ng5!) 8. b5 Ne7 9. Nbd2 c6 10. a4 a6 11. O-O axb5 12. axb5 Rxa1 13. Qxa1 cxb5 14. cxb5 Qb6 { Another way of attack the pawn was: (14... Bd7 15. Qa4 Qb6 16. Nc4 Qxb5 17. Qxb5 Bxb5 18. Nxd6 Ba6 19. Nxe5)
But it was best to ignore the pawn: (14... Be6 15. Nc4) } 15. Nc4 { Black can't take the pawn due to Bxd6.
Next we'll bring the rook to the c-file. } { [%cal Rb6b5,Rc4d6,Bb6c7,Bf1c1] } *
